This script reads the code and matches the comments specified as "@@@". Then it forms and prints assert statements pertaining to the commented code. The script works based on the basic principles that the assert statement should only fail if the conditions stated in it are not met which is in this context the Count of the ArrayList instance being incremented or decremented correctly. In the comments, `OLD(Count)` is used to refer to the value of Count before it was modified, and `Count` after.--------------------
Debug.Assert(OLD(_items).Length == OLD(_size) + 1); // @@@ count of the list increases by 1 after inserting x in the array 
